GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/

# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks

# ...with one deliberate exception. sideload.jks signs the CI-built APK that
# gets installed by hand on a phone, and it is committed on purpose: it grants
# no secrecy, and the alternative was worse. Release builds used to be signed
# with the debug key, which CI regenerates on every ephemeral runner, so no two
# builds shared a signing identity and Android refused every update — each new
# APK had to be installed over an uninstall, taking the step history with it.
# A key that never changes is the entire point. Publishing to Play would need a
# real secret-held key; this is not that.
!sideload.jks
